        "id": 222536,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-27T13:36:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trumpet of Doom\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Trumpet of Doom:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Mint, 21/24/24. I’m amused by TakeWalker’s comment that in his game, Wraith was giving Legacy a bunch of extra cards to play, since in mine, Legacy spent most of the game giving Wraith extra plays.<br><br>\nI’m not sure she really needed them, since by her third turn she had an IR Eyepiece, a Throwing Knives, and a Utility Belt and those were the powers she used for most of the rest of the game, but it was a bit satisfying to end with a 10-card Inventory Barrage.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think most other people go straight for the Eyepiece, whereas I go straight for “what can I pair with Micro-Targeting Computer?” I did zero deck manipulation in that game and came out just fine. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
