      {
        "id": 222537,
        "name": "FearLord",
        "username": "FearLord",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/5f8ce5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-27T14:07:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div>\n\t<b>Trumpet of Doom wrote:</b><br>\n\t<blockquote>\n\t\tMint, 21/24/24. I'm amused by TakeWalker's comment that in his game, Wraith was giving Legacy a bunch of extra cards to play, since in mine, Legacy spent most of the game giving Wraith extra plays.<br>\n\t\tI'm not sure she really needed them, since by her third turn she had an IR Eyepiece, a Throwing Knives, and a Utility Belt and those were the powers she used for most of the rest of the game, but it was a bit satisfying to end with a 10-card Inventory Barrage.\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<pre><code>&lt;/blockquote&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</blockquote></div>\n<p>I think most other people go straight for the Eyepiece, whereas I go straight for “what can I pair with Micro-Targeting Computer?” I did zero deck manipulation in that game and came out just fine. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Same, but I didn’t think about the possibility of Shu coming out and making it unwinnable. I probably would have gone for Eye Piece a bit quicker if I’d have considered that, but Legacy can set up defensively quickly in this fight and also start piling on the damage pretty quick, and by the end I had Wraith dealing 4 to 3 targets and another 4 from her stun bolt as well as some big punches from Legacy and whatever arrows Parse had lying around. I completely ignored the environment and takedown stalled the villain deck quite a bit so we just powered through really with only Atum coming in…</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
