      {
        "id": 222538,
        "name": "Servoret",
        "username": "Servoret",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/91b2a8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-10-07T14:33:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I got this on the first try also. I was shocked when I had already pulled deck manipulation cards for both Parse and Wraith by the time my Take Downs had run out. I figured for sure the twist was going to be that all those cards were buried in their decks, making this a pure damage race before Shu came out. And then for a while I kept expecting all the extra god cards to be clumped up to make pulls unavoidable either way, but I buried the only one I saw.</p>\n<p>The equipment blow up on top would have at least been a nasty surprise for Wraith at the end of the Take Downs, but I avoided it. And the environment deck got to attack for all of one turn before I ended the game. I finished with everybody in the high teens, despite ignoring all of Legacy’s defense cards to focus on the race. So this was a romp for me pretty early on, but I still enjoyed it.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
